                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "17628907",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198028091020",
                            "num_reviews": 244,
                            "playtime_forever": 247,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 226,
                            "last_played": 1440280509
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "City Quest is a hilarious point & click game where you get to play as a dumbass hillbilly.\nA Gameplay & Review video showcasing the features I'm about to talk about:\nhttps://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BG4GjzcM-es\nThis game is reminiscent of older point and clicks like King's Quest, except it focuses more on humor.\nYou can interact with almost everything in multiple different ways.\nThere's a look, use, lick/eat/talk action. All of them come up with unique and well written dialogue for any character or object you click on.\n\nYou will die a lot in this game, it comes with the curious nature of your disconnected stupid hillbilly brain. Because you interact with so many different things in dangerous ways. E.g: Walking into a plane turbine, going up to a carnivorous plant or standing next to a nude man with a huge dong (Don't ask how that one kills you. Watch the video)\n\nThe music is really catchy, and accompanies your journey and mini-games (that once unlocked, you can replay) very well.\n\nHere's one of my highlights: I searched a vending machine. I found an abandoned baby. I got an achievement for it. I put the baby back, and got an achievement for re-abandoning an abandoned baby. I then took it back out, and ate it.\n\nRecommended!",
